CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ reference cast succeeds: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ bad_cast thrown: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [expr.dynamic.cast]/10: a failed cast to reference type throws an
exception matching a std::bad_cast handler.  The front end converted the
reference statically, so dynamic_cast<B &>(rc) on a C object returned a
reference to it as a B (bin53).  The run-time check of the pointer cast is
now applied to &v, and a null result throws a std::bad_cast temporary (if
<typeinfo> declared it; otherwise the static conversion remains).  g++ 13
and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG
assertion.
